---
// src/pages/working-together.astro
status: 'published';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Working Together: From Idea to Website';
const description =
  'How website projects can begin: with a conversation, a private draft, a prototype, or a clear path from idea to launch.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section
    class="bg-gradient-to-b from-stone-50 dark:from-gray-900 to-white dark:to-gray-950 py-20 md:py-28"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
        <div>
          <p
            class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 mb-2"
          >
            Working Together
          </p>

          <h1
            class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-5"
          >
            From idea to website
          </h1>

          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Sometimes the easiest way to discuss an idea is to make it visible.
            A sketch, prototype, or draft website can reveal possibilities that
            are difficult to describe in words alone.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hidden md:flex justify-end">
          <img
            src="/images/shared/SubtleCircles.webp"
            alt="Exploring possibilities through structure and iteration"
            class="w-full max-w-sm object-contain rounded-xl shadow-sm ring-1 ring-stone-200 dark:ring-stone-800"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main content -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">
      <!-- Two ways we begin -->
      <section>
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
        >
          Two ways we begin
        </h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl mb-6">
          Sometimes you reach out with an idea. Sometimes I notice an
          opportunity and share a draft. Either way, the goal is the same: to
          explore what would genuinely help and whether it is worth building.
        </p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              You reach out
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              You have an idea, a challenge, or a website that no longer
              reflects the work behind it. We talk through what the site should
              accomplish, who it serves, and what a useful first version might
              look like.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              I share a draft
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              Occasionally I come across a business, project, or organization
              that sparks my imagination. If I create a private concept, it is
              because I see genuine potential and believe there may be a
              worthwhile opportunity to explore.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Why start with a draft -->
      <section
        class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6 md:p-8 bg-stone-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/40"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
        >
          Why start with a draft?
        </h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-4">
          Many people discover what they want by reacting to something concrete.
          A draft creates a shared reference point. It turns abstract
          conversations into practical ones.
        </p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <div
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-5 bg-white/80 dark:bg-gray-950/50"
          >
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              What feels right here?
            </p>
          </div>

          <div
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-5 bg-white/80 dark:bg-gray-950/50"
          >
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">What feels missing?</p>
          </div>

          <div
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-5 bg-white/80 dark:bg-gray-950/50"
          >
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              What should this communicate?
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mt-4">
          A draft is not the answer. It is a tool for thinking.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Private by default -->
      <section
        class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6 md:p-8"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
        >
          Private by default
        </h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl">
          Drafts are shared through private links and are not indexed by search
          engines. They are intended for the people involved in the project and
          provide a quiet space to explore ideas, gather feedback, and make
          decisions before anything becomes public.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Ways we can work together -->
      <section>
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
        >
          Ways we can work together
        </h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Prototype
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              A focused concept that explores structure, language, and direction
              before larger decisions are made.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Build
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              A complete website designed around the goals of the project and
              the people it serves.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Collaborate
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              A shared process where we shape decisions together and you remain
              closely involved throughout.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Stewardship
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              Ongoing improvements, updates, and refinements as the website
              evolves.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Handoff
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              A completed site with guidance, documentation, and a clear
              transition so you can manage it independently.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Referral
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              If a project needs deeper development, complex ecommerce, or a
              custom app, I can help clarify the need and point toward a
              specialist.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The goal -->
      <section
        class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6 md:p-8 bg-stone-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/40"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
        >
          The goal
        </h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl mb-4">
          The goal is not simply to launch a website. The goal is to create
          something that reflects the quality of your work, helps people
          understand what you do, and supports the next stage of the journey.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl">
          Sometimes that begins with a conversation. Sometimes it begins with a
          draft. Either way, we start by making the idea visible.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <section
        class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6 md:p-8 bg-white/70 dark:bg-gray-900/40"
      >
        <div
          class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4"
        >
          <div>
            <h2
              class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
            >
              Ready to explore an idea?
            </h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              Bring a rough concept, an existing website, or just the sense that
              something could work better.
            </p>
          </div>

          <a
            href="https://danryanneff.com/contact/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-block text-sm font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 text-gray-900 dark:text-white hover:no-underline"
          >
            Book a meeting
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
